      {
        "number": 9,
        "internalPageId": null,
        "title": "To Consider 1. Adjectives that finish in -ING are normally used to describe situations or things. 2. Adjectives that finish in -ED are used to describe how people feel because of something. 3. Adjectives may be unique or classified into a pattern. E.G.: Glib / Silly / Tiny 4. Some -ING adjectives are used to describe people if they are producing something in someone else: I am annoyed, you know? Joey is so annoying, always talking too much. 5. Another issue is that some adjectives ending -IC and -ICAL tend to be confusing; here is a list for patterns https://www.thefreedictionary.com/Commonly-Confused-Suffixes-ic-vs-ical.htm#:~:text=The%20suffixes%20%E2%80%9C%2Dic%E2%80%9D%20and,are%20notoriously%20difficult%20to%20distinguish.",
        "visibleTexts": [
